{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-chemistry","topic_code":"1.2","key":"B","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"B","ambiguous":false,"work":"To find the average atomic mass, calculate the weighted average: (68.926 amu × 0.6011) + (70.925 amu × 0.3989). Because the lighter isotope (mass ~69 amu) is more abundant (approx. 60%) than the heavier isotope (mass ~71 amu, approx. 40%), the average must be less than the midpoint (70 amu), specifically close to 69 + 0.40(2) = 69.8 amu, which corresponds to 69.72 amu. Furthermore, isotopes of the same element must have the same number of protons and differ only in their number of neutrons. The mass difference of approximately 2 amu means the heavier isotope has two more neutrons."},"usage":{"inputTokens":348,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":348,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":658,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":197,"reasoningTokens":461},"totalTokens":1006,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":461,"promptTokenCount":348,"candidatesTokenCount":197,"totalTokenCount":1006,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":348}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":197}]},"reasoningTokens":461,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":6347},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":["A full calculation is not required because 69.72 amu is the only numerical option below the unweighted mean (69.93 amu), which aligns well with non-calculator estimation strategies."]},"usage":{"inputTokens":20526,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":20526,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":2146,"outputToke