{"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","subject_key":"ap-chemistry","topic_code":"1.3","key":"D","flags":["rationale_C","needs_figure_or_calculator"],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"D","ambiguous":false,"work":"Assume 100 g sample: 89.94 g C and 10.06 g H. Moles C = 89.94 / 12.01 ≈ 7.49 mol; moles H = 10.06 / 1.008 ≈ 9.98 mol. Divide by smaller: C = 1, H ≈ 1.333 = 4/3, so empirical formula is C3H4. Empirical molar mass = 3(12.01)+4(1.008) ≈ 40.06 g/mol. Molecular mass / empirical mass = 120.2 / 40.06 ≈ 3, so molecular formula = C9H12."},"usage":{"inputTokens":359,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":359,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":601,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":155,"reasoningTokens":446},"totalTokens":960,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":359,"completion_tokens":601,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":359,"total_tokens":960,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":446}},"reasoningTokens":446,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":5072},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":false,"issue":"States that 120.2 ÷ 13.02 ≈ 9, but the quotient is about 9.23, so the described scaling to C₉H₉ is not mathematically supported."},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":true,"style_notes":["Rationales for wrong choices use imperative 'Fix:' coaching language; this is a style choice, not a content defect."]},"usage":{"inputTokens":19732,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":8596,"cacheReadTokens":11136},"outputTokens":8720,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":249,"reasoningTokens":8471},"totalTokens":28452,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":19732,"completion_tokens":8720,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":11136,"prompt_cache_miss_token