{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-chemistry","topic_code":"1.5","key":"A","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"A","ambiguous":false,"work":"Potassium (Z = 19) has the ground-state electron configuration [Ar]4s¹. On the AP exam, simply citing a periodic trend (as in C) does not earn the explanation/reasoning point; students must explain trends in terms of Coulombic attraction, atomic structure, shell distance, and shielding. Choice A correctly identifies the configuration and explains that the 4s electron is in a higher principal energy level (shell), farther from the nucleus, and more shielded, leading to a weaker effective electrostatic attraction and thus a lower first ionization energy."},"usage":{"inputTokens":390,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":390,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":365,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":140,"reasoningTokens":225},"totalTokens":755,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":225,"promptTokenCount":390,"candidatesTokenCount":140,"totalTokenCount":755,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":390}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":140}]},"reasoningTokens":225,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":3872},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":["The stem references earning 'the reasoning point,' using AP exam rubric framing to explicitly test the misconception of citing a trend rather than causal Coulombic reasoning (choice C)."]},"usage":{"inputTokens":20550,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":20550,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":790,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":253,