{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-chemistry","topic_code":"2.1","key":"C","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"C","ambiguous":false,"work":"Calculate the difference in electronegativity (ΔEN) for each bond:\n- S–H: 2.58 - 2.20 = 0.38\n- N–H: 3.04 - 2.20 = 0.84\n- O–H: 3.44 - 2.20 = 1.24\n\nA larger electronegativity difference corresponds to a more polar bond, so the order from least polar to most polar is S–H < N–H < O–H. Since oxygen is more electronegative than hydrogen (3.44 > 2.20), the partial negative charge (δ-) resides on oxygen."},"usage":{"inputTokens":357,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":357,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":400,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":178,"reasoningTokens":222},"totalTokens":757,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":222,"promptTokenCount":357,"candidatesTokenCount":178,"totalTokenCount":757,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":357}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":178}]},"reasoningTokens":222,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":3648},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":20528,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":20528,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":638,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":214,"reasoningTokens":424},"totalTokens":21166,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":424,"promptTokenCount":20528,"candidatesTokenCount":214,"totalTokenCount":21166,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":20528}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":214}]},"reasoningTokens":424,"cachedInputT