{"model":"deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro","subject_key":"ap-chemistry","topic_code":"2.1","key":"C","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"C","ambiguous":false,"work":"Electronegativity differences: S–H = |2.58 - 2.20| = 0.38, N–H = |3.04 - 2.20| = 0.84, O–H = |3.44 - 2.20| = 1.24. Larger difference means more polar, so S–H < N–H < O–H. In O–H, oxygen is more electronegative, so the partial negative charge is on O."},"usage":{"inputTokens":423,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":423,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":375,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":127,"reasoningTokens":248},"totalTokens":798,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":423,"completion_tokens":375,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":423,"total_tokens":798,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":248}},"reasoningTokens":248,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":3699},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":19716,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":8580,"cacheReadTokens":11136},"outputTokens":3595,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":180,"reasoningTokens":3415},"totalTokens":23311,"raw":{"prompt_tokens":19716,"completion_tokens":3595,"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":11136,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":8580,"total_tokens":23311,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":11136},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3415}},"reasoningTokens":3415,"cachedInputTokens":11136},"ms":26717},"at":"2026-10-07T00:36:27.687Z"}
{"model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","subject_key":"ap-chemistry","topic_code":"3.8","key":"C","flags":[],"solve":{"ok":true,"object":{"answer":"C","ambiguous":false,"work":"The concentration is proportional to the number of molecules divided by the volume. The first box has 6 molecules in 0.5 L, which corresponds to a ratio of 12 molecules per liter. For the second box representing 1.5 L to have the same concentration, it must contain 12 molecules/L * 1.5 L = 18 molecules. Alternatively, the volume is 3 times greater (1.5 L / 0.5 L = 3), so it must contain 3 times as many molecules: 6 * 3 = 18."},"usage":{"inputTokens":271,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":271,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":332,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":140,"reasoningTokens":192},"totalTokens":603,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":192,"promptTokenCount":271,"candidatesTokenCount":140,"totalTokenCount":603,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":271}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":140}]},"reasoningTokens":192,"cachedInputTokens":0},"ms":3825},"audit":{"ok":true,"object":{"key_correct":true,"key_issue":"","choices":[{"choice_key":"A","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"B","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"C","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""},{"choice_key":"D","rationale_accurate":true,"issue":""}],"scope_verdict":"fully_in_scope","out_of_scope_concepts":[],"on_topic":true,"needs_figure_or_calculator":false,"style_notes":[]},"usage":{"inputTokens":20423,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":20423,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":681,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":214,"reasoningTokens":467},"totalTokens":21104,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":467,"promptTokenCount":20423,"candidatesTokenCount":214,"totalTokenCount":21104,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":20423}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":214}]},"reasoningT